  - Key: ultra.blood-moon.name
    Values:
    - Blood Moon
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.blood-moon.description
    Values:
    - The moon comes up red, and every hand in the party is stronger for what he
      bled.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.death-mark.name
    Values:
    - Death Mark
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.death-mark.description
    Values:
    - She picks the one that dies first, and everyone can see it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.demon-form.name
    Values:
    - Demon Form
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.demon-form.description
    Values:
    - The Warlock lets the thing he bargains with wear him for a while.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.divine-intervention.name
    Values:
    - Divine Intervention
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.divine-intervention.description
    Values:
    - He steps between an ally and the blow, takes it at half weight, and answers
      in kind.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.earthsplitter.name
    Values:
    - Earthsplitter
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.earthsplitter.description
    Values:
    - Everything he has built up goes into one blow, and the floor splits under all
      of them.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.flamethrower-mech.name
    Values:
    - Flamethrower Mech
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.flamethrower-mech.description
    Values:
    - She bolts together a flamethrower mech and climbs on. It sets the whole room
      alight.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.flurry.name
    Values:
    - Flurry
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.flurry.description
    Values:
    - He stops guarding and simply swings, again and again, at whatever is closest.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.grand-heist.name
    Values:
    - Grand Heist
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.grand-heist.description
    Values:
    - Every pocket in the room, in one pass.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.judgement-day.name
    Values:
    - Judgement Day
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.judgement-day.description
    Values:
    - Light falls on every enemy at once. The dead get no second chance.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.lay-on-hands.name
    Values:
    - Lay on Hands
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.lay-on-hands.description
    Values:
    - His hands on one ally, and everything wrong with them is put right.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.mass-hysteria.name
    Values:
    - Mass Hysteria
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.mass-hysteria.description
    Values:
    - A whisper in every head at once. Half of them believe it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.miracle-of-hope.name
    Values:
    - Miracle of Hope
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.miracle-of-hope.description
    Values:
    - A prayer for the long road. Everyone finds a little more in reserve.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.miracle-of-light.name
    Values:
    - Miracle of Light
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.miracle-of-light.description
    Values:
    - She asks, and is answered. Wounds close and every curse lifts.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.miracle-of-righteousness.name
    Values:
    - Miracle of Righteousness
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.miracle-of-righteousness.description
    Values:
    - Judgement falls on every enemy, and what should already be dead is made so.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.multi-cast.name
    Values:
    - MultiCast
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.multi-cast.description
    Values:
    - 'Focus spent all at once: the next ability again, and again, and again.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.oil-spewing-mech.name
    Values:
    - Oil Spewing Mech
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.oil-spewing-mech.description
    Values:
    - She bolts together an oil-spewing walker and climbs on. Everything it hits
      is oiled - and oil burns.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.pack-hunt.name
    Values:
    - Pack Hunt
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.pack-hunt.description
    Values:
    - Three grey shapes go through the line, and come back red.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.pin-down.name
    Values:
    - Pin Down
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.pin-down.description
    Values:
    - Arrows through boots, sleeves and shadows. Nobody is going anywhere soon.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.rain-of-arrows.name
    Values:
    - Rain of Arrows
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.rain-of-arrows.description
    Values:
    - Five arrows, five targets he never had to aim at.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.rain-of-fire.name
    Values:
    - Rain of Fire
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.rain-of-fire.description
    Values:
    - The sky opens on the Warlock's word and the room burns.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.sacrifice.name
    Values:
    - Sacrifice
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.sacrifice.description
    Values:
    - The Cultist gives an ally to what he serves. What comes back is still on your
      side - mostly.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.smoke-and-mirrors.name
    Values:
    - Smoke and Mirrors
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.smoke-and-mirrors.description
    Values:
    - Smoke, and somewhere in it the party - or a dozen copies of it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.soul-harvest.name
    Values:
    - Soul Harvest
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.soul-harvest.description
    Values:
    - Every soul in the room pays a tithe, and the Warlock collects.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.take-cover.name
    Values:
    - Take Cover
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.take-cover.description
    Values:
    - '"Down!" The whole line braces behind his shield until the worst has passed.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.warrior-mech.name
    Values:
    - Warrior Mech
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: ultra.warrior-mech.description
    Values:
    - She bolts together a brawling mech and climbs on. It takes the blows meant
      for her.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.abyssal-nightmare.name
    Values:
    - Abyssal Nightmare
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.abyssal-nightmare.description
    Values:
    - No eyes. Only the mouth, and the teeth, and the teeth inside the teeth.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.aegis-lion.name
    Values:
    - Aegis Lion
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.aegis-lion.description
    Values:
    - A lion of hammered light plants itself before the Paladin and roars. The enemies
      turn on the Paladin, and the Paladin hardens to meet them.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.archon.name
    Values:
    - Archon
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.archon.description
    Values:
    - A figure of light takes the party's place. It does not strike so much as judge.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.auto-turret.name
    Values:
    - Auto Turret
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.auto-turret.description
    Values:
    - A brass tripod with a rivet gun on top and a boiler underneath. She sets it
      down, opens the valve and lets it work.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.bloodfang-boar.name
    Values:
    - Bloodfang Boar
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.bloodfang-boar.description
    Values:
    - A primal war boar charges onto the field and bellows. Every hero's Strength
      rises by half.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.blood-idol.name
    Values:
    - Blood Idol
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.blood-idol.description
    Values:
    - A shape of clotted red, raised from what the Cultist bleeds. It feeds the party,
      and the enemy hates it for it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.cairn-golem.name
    Values:
    - Cairn Golem
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.cairn-golem.description
    Values:
    - The stones of an old cairn rise and take the party's place. It takes every
      blow meant for them, and the one that breaks it goes no further.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.dark-twin.name
    Values:
    - Dark Twin
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.dark-twin.description
    Values:
    - Her shadow, stepped off the wall, faster than she is.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.dawn-stag.name
    Values:
    - Dawn Stag
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.dawn-stag.description
    Values:
    - A white stag steps out of the morning. Where its light falls, wounds close,
      and keep closing.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.demon-army.name
    Values:
    - Demon Army
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.demon-army.description
    Values:
    - The Warlock opens the way and his demons pour through, taking the party's place
      until the bargain runs out.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.exatrix.name
    Values:
    - Exatrix
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.exatrix.description
    Values:
    - A shade of something that hunted before there were names takes the party's
      place. Every wound she opens costs the enemy time.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.flamethrower-mech.name
    Values:
    - Flamethrower Mech
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.flamethrower-mech.description
    Values:
    - Fuel tanks, a pilot light and a very long nozzle. It keeps its distance and
      sets the room alight.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.galewing.name
    Values:
    - Galewing
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.galewing.description
    Values:
    - A great hawk drops out of nowhere and rakes every enemy twice, finding the
      gaps in their guard.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.glacius.name
    Values:
    - Glacius
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.glacius.description
    Values:
    - A frost bear. One claw rimes an enemy in ice, ready for the party's water;
      its breath hardens the party's skin.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.golden-ferret.name
    Values:
    - Golden Ferret
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.golden-ferret.description
    Values:
    - It finds the loose coin in every pocket, and the party's luck turns with it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.grey-fang.name
    Values:
    - Grey Fang
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.grey-fang.description
    Values:
    - The Ranger's hound. It runs down what he marks.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.guardian-angel.name
    Values:
    - Guardian Angel
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.guardian-angel.description
    Values:
    - Wings close around the whole party. For a while, the blows have to get through
      her first.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.horror.name
    Values:
    - Horror
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.horror.description
    Values:
    - 'What the rite leaves of a hero: everything they were, turned outward.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.ifrit.name
    Values:
    - Ifrit
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.ifrit.description
    Values:
    - A fire spirit takes the party's place. When it goes, fallen or sent away, it
      takes the field with it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.imp.name
    Values:
    - Imp
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.imp.description
    Values:
    - 'A cackling scrap of the pit, bound to the Warlock''s blood. The Demon Army''s
      rank and file: frail, fast, and full of fire.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.iron-charger.name
    Values:
    - Iron Charger
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.iron-charger.description
    Values:
    - A barded warhorse that comes through the enemy line like a door through a wall.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.judgement-seraph.name
    Values:
    - Judgement Seraph
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.judgement-seraph.description
    Values:
    - A winged knight takes the party's place. It hits far harder than it can be
      hit, and the blow that finally breaks it goes no further.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.murder-of-crows.name
    Values:
    - Murder of Crows
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.murder-of-crows.description
    Values:
    - A black cloud of wings and beaks that goes for the eyes.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.oil-mech.name
    Values:
    - Oil Spewing Mech
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.oil-mech.description
    Values:
    - A squat walker with a drum of machine oil on its back. Everything it touches
      slows down - and catches fire easily.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.phoenix.name
    Values:
    - Phoenix
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.phoenix.description
    Values:
    - A bird of white fire passes over the line. The fallen rise in its wake, and
      the standing breathe easier.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.qyraxis.name
    Values:
    - Qyraxis
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.qyraxis.description
    Values:
    - A bird made of the storm itself. It strikes every enemy twice, and they move
      like they are wading.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.succubus.name
    Values:
    - Succubus
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.succubus.description
    Values:
    - A demoness of the deep circles, an Imp the Warlock's bargains have raised.
      She holds the line with whip and glamour.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.warrior-mech.name
    Values:
    - Warrior Mech
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.warrior-mech.description
    Values:
    - Brass plate, piston fists and a boiler for a heart. It hits hard and takes
      harder.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.watcher.name
    Values:
    - The Watcher
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.watcher.description
    Values:
    - Something from below the deep comes up to look. What it sees, it unmakes.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.writhing-spawn.name
    Values:
    - Writhing Spawn
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: summon.writhing-spawn.description
    Values:
    - A knot of the deep that came when he called. It holds things in place.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.conductor-3d-4c-5b-6a.name
    Values:
    - Conductor
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.conductor-3d-4c-5b-6a.description
    Values:
    - Lightning arcs through metal for doubled impact!
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.freeze-2e-3d-4c-5b.name
    Values:
    - Freeze
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.freeze-2e-3d-4c-5b.description
    Values:
    - Ice and water combine to freeze the enemy solid.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.ignite-1f-2e-3d-4c.name
    Values:
    - Ignite
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.infection-4c-5b-6a-79.name
    Values:
    - Infection
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: combo.infection-4c-5b-6a-79.description
    Values:
    - Poison seeps into physical wounds, sapping all strength.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: set.shadowweave.name
    Values:
    - Shadowweave
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: set.shadowweave.tier-1.text
    Values:
    - +10% Shadow damage
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: set.shadowweave.tier-2.text
    Values:
    - +5% Intelligence
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: set.shadowweave.tier-3.text
    Values:
    - Every ability also deals 10% of its power as Shadow damage
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.ashen-deep.name
    Values:
    - The Ashen Deep
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.ashen-deep.description
    Values:
    - The water gave out and the rock began to weep heat. Something under the March
      has been burning for a long time.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.ashen-deep.level-1.name
    Values:
    - Cinder Gate
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.ashen-deep.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Slag Halls
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.ashen-deep.level-3.name
    Values:
    - Emberfall
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.name
    Values:
    - The Blood Stair
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.description
    Values:
    - A cult carved this stair down to its altar, and its last initiate is still
      chained at the bottom. Five floors, none of them kind. Most parties turn back.
      Some don't have to.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.level-1.name
    Values:
    - The Bleeding Steps
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Chapel of Knives
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.level-3.name
    Values:
    - The Ossuary Gate
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.level-4.name
    Values:
    - The Red Cloister
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.blood-stair.level-5.name
    Values:
    - The Altar of the Last Initiate
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.catacombs.name
    Values:
    - The Catacombs
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.catacombs.description
    Values:
    - Below the Archive the dead were stacked, not buried. Somebody has taught them
      to stand back up.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.catacombs.level-1.name
    Values:
    - The Ossuary Stair
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.catacombs.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Bone Galleries
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.catacombs.level-3.name
    Values:
    - The Lich's Sepulchre
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-chapel.name
    Values:
    - The Drowned Chapel
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-chapel.description
    Values:
    - A chapel went down with the March, bells and all. Pump the nave low enough
      and the door at the bottom opens again - and someone behind it is still singing.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-chapel.level-1.name
    Values:
    - The Flooded Nave
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-chapel.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Drowned Choir
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.name
    Values:
    - The Drowned March
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.description
    Values:
    - The water that filled the lower halls came from somewhere. Something down there
      is still breathing.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.level-1.name
    Values:
    - Silt Shallows
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Reedcage
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.level-3.name
    Values:
    - The Weeping Causeway
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.level-4.name
    Values:
    - Rotwater Deep
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.drowned-march.level-5.name
    Values:
    - The Mire Throne
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.hollow-vault.name
    Values:
    - The Hollow Vault
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.hollow-vault.description
    Values:
    - The Hoarder was counting for someone. There is a door behind the ledger.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.hollow-vault.level-1.name
    Values:
    - The Hollow Vault
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.sealed-archive.name
    Values:
    - The Sealed Archive
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.sealed-archive.description
    Values:
    - A library the dungeon walled up rather than burn. Something in the stacks is
      still reading - and someone locked in with it is still casting.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.sealed-archive.level-1.name
    Values:
    - The Ash Stacks
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.sealed-archive.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Broken Orrery
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.seeping-cistern.name
    Values:
    - The Seeping Cistern
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.seeping-cistern.description
    Values:
    - Under the Warrens the old cistern has turned to something that eats. The cutpurse
      ran down there with your purse. Something down there caught them.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.seeping-cistern.level-1.name
    Values:
    - The Sump
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.seeping-cistern.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Mother Pool
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.tutorial-run.name
    Values:
    - The Threshold
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.tutorial-run.description
    Values:
    - 'Where every hero starts: four floors down, and a prisoner worth freeing.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.tutorial-run.level-1.name
    Values:
    - Dungeon Entrance
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.tutorial-run.level-2.name
    Values:
    - Upper Halls
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.tutorial-run.level-3.name
    Values:
    - Collapsed Caverns
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.tutorial-run.level-4.name
    Values:
    - Sunken Depths
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.the-warrens.name
    Values:
    - The Warrens
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.the-warrens.description
    Values:
    - 'A standing contract: clear the vault tunnels, keep what you carry out. The
      hoard always grows back.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.the-warrens.level-1.name
    Values:
    - Warren Tunnels
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: run.the-warrens.level-2.name
    Values:
    - The Counting Room
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.bestiary.name
    Values:
    - Hall of Knowledge
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.bestiary.description
    Values:
    - Everything the party has survived, and everything the Forge could make, written
      down.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.campfire.name
    Values:
    - Campfire
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.campfire.description
    Values:
    - Four seats and a low fire. Who marches out is decided here.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.campfire.level-1.grant
    Values:
    - The run's XP is split evenly between everyone who marches out.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.campfire.level-2.grant
    Values:
    - 'Mentor: name a hero and they take a double share of every kill.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.campfire.level-3.grant
    Values:
    - 'Catch Up: the double share goes to whoever is furthest behind.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.forge.name
    Values:
    - Forge
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.forge.description
    Values:
    - Bring a recipe, the stuff it calls for and the gold for the fire. Essence still
      hardens a combo.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.forge.level-1.grant
    Values:
    - Forge combos up to Lv 1.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.forge.level-2.grant
    Values:
    - Forge combos up to Lv 3.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.forge.level-3.grant
    Values:
    - Forge combos up to Lv 5, as far as the craft goes.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.merchant.name
    Values:
    - Merchant
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.merchant.description
    Values:
    - Gear, potions, and a keen sense of what you can afford.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.sphere-hall.name
    Values:
    - Hall of Progression
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.sphere-hall.description
    Values:
    - Where a hero decides what they are becoming.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.storehouse.name
    Values:
    - Storehouse
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: building.storehouse.description
    Values:
    - Gear, abilities, potions and the raw stuff you dragged home.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.title
    Values:
    - A Shaft in the Ceiling
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.prompt
    Values:
    - A shaft opens in the ceiling well above head height, and something on the ledge
      up there catches what little light there is. The wall under it is damp and
      crumbling, with just enough to hold on to.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Climb for it
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - Three quick holds and you are on the ledge. Somebody stashed this up here and
      never came back for it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-1.success-2.text
    Values:
    - You get up, get a hand on it, and get back down before the wall gives. Coin,
      and nothing else worth the climb.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-1.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - The wall lets go halfway up. You land badly and stay landed for a while.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-1.failure-2.text
    Values:
    - You bring most of the wall down with you, and the noise brings something else.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Leave whatever it is up there
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.ceiling-shaft.option-2.decline
    Values:
    - Whatever is on the ledge can stay on the ledge.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.title
    Values:
    - A Choked Passage
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.prompt
    Values:
    - Half the ceiling has come down across a side passage, and the draught coming
      through the gap smells of open air rather than more dungeon. The top slab is
      the only thing holding the rest up. Somebody could get a shoulder under it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Get a shoulder under it
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - 'You take the weight long enough for the rest of the party to clear the gap,
      and what is behind it: a dead porter, still carrying.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-1.success-2.text
    Values:
    - You hold it. It costs you something to hold it, and the passage behind is empty
      besides a dropped purse.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-1.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - The slab shifts the wrong way and the rest of it follows. Everyone comes out
      of the dust coughing and bleeding.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-1.failure-2.text
    Values:
    - It settles onto your back before you can get clear. Nothing broken - but nothing
      works quite right for a while either.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Leave the passage blocked
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.choked-passage.option-2.decline
    Values:
    - The draught is not worth the ceiling. You go the long way.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.title
    Values:
    - A Cutpurse on the Rope
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.prompt
    Values:
    - 'Every lock in these tunnels was picked before you reached it. Now you know
      by whom: someone hangs from a frayed rope over the counting-pit, one hand on
      the line and the other still holding a purse that is not theirs. ''Evening,''
      they say. ''I don''t suppose you''d pull?'''
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Catch the rope
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - You get a hand on the line as it parts and haul them over the lip. They look
      at you, then at the tunnel, then hand the purse back. 'Fine. You'll want someone
      who can open things.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.option-1.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - The rope goes. So does the cutpurse - not down, but sideways into a crawlway
      you never saw, and a little heavier than before.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Leave them hanging
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.cutpurse.option-2.decline
    Values:
    - '''Suit yourselves,'' they call after you. ''I''ll be around.'''
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.title
    Values:
    - A Drowned Offering
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.prompt
    Values:
    - 'Knee-deep in the standing water, a stone bowl still holds its offering: coins,
      teeth, something folded in oilcloth. The water around it is warmer than the
      water around your boots.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Kneel and say the words
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - The warmth comes up out of the bowl and goes through all of you. Old wounds
      close over. Whatever is owed here has been paid before.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-1.success-2.text
    Values:
    - Nothing answers, but the folded oilcloth is worth having.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-1.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - You get the words wrong. The water goes cold, the taste of it gets into everyone,
      and the whole party feels thinner for it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-1.failure-2.text
    Values:
    - The bowl tips. Something in the reeds decides it has been insulted.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Take the coins and go
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-2.success-1.text
    Values:
    - You pocket the coins without ceremony. The water stays cold behind you the
      whole way out.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-3.label
    Values:
    - Leave the bowl alone
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.drowned-offering.option-3.decline
    Values:
    - You keep your hands to yourself and wade on past.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.title
    Values:
    - A Musty Tome
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.prompt
    Values:
    - A swollen leather tome lies open on a lectern, its pages furred with mould
      and strung across with old web. Whatever is written in it was worth writing
      down carefully. Something has been living in the spine for a long time.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Ease it off the lectern
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - You lift the cover clear, copy what matters, and leave the rest to the damp.
      A collector will pay for this.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-1.success-2.text
    Values:
    - You get the pages out intact - and the thing in the spine gets a piece of you
      on the way past.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-1.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - The spine splits, the web comes alive, and something long-legged sinks its
      jaws in before you can pull back. The pages are ruined.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-1.failure-2.text
    Values:
    - The lectern gives way. You come out of the mess with nothing but a lighter
      pack.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Leave it to rot
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.musty-tome.option-2.decline
    Values:
    - You leave the book to the damp. It has waited this long; it can wait longer.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.title
    Values:
    - A Sealed Tomb
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.prompt
    Values:
    - A slab of stone has been dragged over a hole in the cavern floor and mortared
      down at the edges. Somebody wanted this shut. The mortar is old, and the slab
      has a lip you could get your hands under.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Heave the slab aside
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - 'The mortar goes with a crack and the slab slides. Below: a body in good armour
      that has not needed it for a century.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-1.success-2.text
    Values:
    - It shifts far enough. You come up with a sword and a badly wrenched shoulder.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-1.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - The slab comes back on your fingers and the whole cavern hears about it. Whatever
      was sealed in was not the only thing down here.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-1.failure-2.text
    Values:
    - It will not move. You leave skin on the stone for nothing.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Leave the dead sealed
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.sealed-tomb.option-2.decline
    Values:
    - Somebody mortared this down for a reason. You leave the reason where it is.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.title
    Values:
    - The Treasury
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.prompt
    Values:
    - Strongboxes line the walls, prised open and emptied a long time ago. There
      is loose coin in the corners for anyone patient enough to go along the shelves
      - and one gilded chest, lock already sprung, that nobody has touched.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-1.label
    Values:
    - Gather the loose coin
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-1.success-1.text
    Values:
    - You work along the shelves and come away with a respectable double handful.
      The gilded chest is still sitting there, still untouched, as you leave.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-2.label
    Values:
    - Throw the lid back on the gilded chest
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-2.success-1.text
    Values:
    - 'The lid swings clear of a needle you never saw. Underneath: coin, and gear
      somebody else did not live to use.'
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-2.success-2.text
    Values:
    - Empty, but for a fat purse wedged under the lining.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-2.failure-1.text
    Values:
    - The needle goes in above the knuckle. Whatever was on it burns all the way
      up the arm, and does not stop burning.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-2.failure-2.text
    Values:
    - The lid comes back on a spring and the crack of it goes down every corridor
      on this floor. Something answers.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-3.label
    Values:
    - Take nothing and move on
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: event.treasury-hoard.option-3.decline
    Values:
    - You leave the shelves and the chest exactly as you found them.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.retry-first-floor.text
    Values:
    - The dungeon is still waiting. Take The Story to go back down.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.build-hall-in-town.text
    Values:
    - You came home with timber. Click the Hall of Progression's foundation to raise
      it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.build-hall-on-panel.text
    Values:
    - Build the Hall of Progression. It costs the timber you just brought home.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.open-hall-in-town.text
    Values:
    - The hall stands. Step inside to spend the XP your hero gained.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.enter-hall-on-panel.text
    Values:
    - The hall stands. Enter it to spend the XP your hero gained.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.pick-node.text
    Values:
    - Every fight gave your hero XP. Click the glowing node - you can afford it.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.activate-node.text
    Values:
    - Now press Activate to spend the XP.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.node-learned.text
    Values:
    - Your hero grew stronger. Head back to town - the road down is open again.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.take-the-road.text
    Values:
    - The town is yours now. When you are ready, take The Story to continue The Threshold.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.first-death.text
    Values:
    - Every party falls, and falling is how you get stronger. What you earned on
      earlier floors is safe - spend it in town, then go back down.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.open-storehouse-in-town.text
    Values:
    - The floor paid out a sword. Gear is vital to survival down there - open the
      Storehouse and put it on.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.enter-storehouse-on-panel.text
    Values:
    - Enter the Storehouse. Everything you bring home is kept here.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.equip-gear.text
    Values:
    - Pick the Main Hand slot, then the sword, and equip it. A party without gear
      does not last long.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.gear-equipped.text
    Values:
    - Equipped. Check here after every run - better gear turns up the deeper you
      go. Back to town when ready.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.go-on.text
    Values:
    - Your party is armed. When you are ready, take The Story to continue The Threshold.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.challenge-ahead.text
    Values:
    - Not every open road is meant for you yet. {run} is built for a far stronger
      party - most go elsewhere first.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.revisit-hall-in-town.text
    Values:
    - Both heroes earned XP on that floor. Visit the Hall of Progression - the Paladin
      can grow too.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: tutorial.revisit-hall-on-grid.text
    Values:
    - The Paladin has XP to spend as well. Spend it on either hero, or go back when
      you are ready.
    Reviewed: 0
    Note: 
  - Key: node.mage-multicast.name
    Values:
    - MultiCast
